	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "The compute module's bay on a host board, with the compute link's socket (boards/contracts/compute-link.md sections 3-4, 2026-11-27): the module (70 x 70 mm) stands over it on four M3 standoffs (11.0 mm), its 2 x 20 header plugged into the 2 x 20 2.54 mm socket strip here (pads 1-40, through-hole, body 8.51 mm). Four NPTH 3.2 mm holes at the module's corner holes (60.6 mm square pattern) with the 8.4 mm copper keep-out. UNLIKE the network module's bay, host parts may sit under the module up to 8.65 mm tall: the courtyard is the socket and the four keep-outs only; F.Fab is the module's outline, User.1 the height-limited area. STAGED for the owner to install.")
